<title>PAKISTAN: CRICKET-PAKISTAN TO HOST FOUR-NATION JUBILEE CONTEST.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-PAKISTAN TO HOST FOUR-NATION JUBILEE CONTEST.</headline>
<dateline>LAHORE, Pakistan 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka, West Indies and South Africa will play in a four-nation cricket tournament in Pakistan in November, organisers said on Monday.</p>
<p>They will take part in a one-day series marking Pakistan's golden jubilee in Lahore from November 1 to 8.</p>
<p>South Africa and West Indies will also play three-test series against Pakistan between October and early December, the Pakistan Cricket Board (PCB) said.</p>
<p>Test schedule:</p>
<p>Pakistan v South Africa</p>
<p>October 6-10, Rawalpindi</p>
<p>October 17-21, Shiekhupura</p>
<p>October 24-28, Faisalabad</p>
<p>Pakistan v West Indies</p>
<p>November 17-21, Peshawar</p>
<p>November 29-December 3, Gujranwala</p>
<p>December 6-10, Karachi.</p>
</text>
